        "cap": "A parrot on a stool chatters nonstop while a man covers his eyes."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>dict</b> = <b>say</b>. <b>loqu</b>, <b>locut</b> = <b>speak</b>. <b>voc</b>, <b>vok</b> = <b>call, voice</b>. <b>nounce</b> = <b>announce, report</b>. <b>mand</b> = <b>order</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "The <i>loqu</i> words are about how a person talks: <b>loquacious</b> (talking a lot), <b>eloquent</b> (speaking out well), <b>colloquial</b> (the way people talk together, informal), <b>soliloquy</b> (speaking alone, as an actor does on stage). The <i>voc</i> words are about calling out: <b>vociferous</b> means carrying a loud voice."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "dict",
            "loqu",
            "voc"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on dict, loqu and voc."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "nounce",
            "mand"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "nounce (announce) and mand (order)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>diction</b><br>the choice of words; also, how clearly words are spoken",
            "<b>dict</b> <i>say</i> + -ion<br>→ “a way of saying”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>edict</b><br>an official order from an authority",
            "e- <i>out</i> + <b>dict</b> <i>say</i><br>→ “a thing said out (by those in charge)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>verdict</b><br>a decision or judgment, especially a jury’s",
            "ver <i>true</i> + <b>dict</b> <i>say</i><br>→ “a true saying”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>eloquent</b><br>speaking or writing in a fluent, moving way",
            "e- <i>out</i> + <b>loqu</b> <i>speak</i> + -ent<br>→ “speaking out (well)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>colloquial</b><br>used in ordinary, informal conversation",
            "col- <i>together</i> + <b>loqu</b> <i>speak</i> + -ial<br>→ “speaking together (everyday talk)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>soliloquy</b><br>a speech in a play in which a character speaks thoughts aloud alone",
            "sol <i>alone</i> + <b>loqu</b> <i>speak</i> + -y<br>→ “speaking alone”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>advocate</b><br>to speak in favor of",
            "ad- <i>to</i> + <b>voc</b> <i>call</i> + -ate<br>→ “call to (someone’s side)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>vociferous</b><br>loud and forceful in expressing opinions",
            "<b>voc</b> <i>voice</i> + fer <i>carry</i> + -ous<br>→ “carrying the voice (loudly)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>denounce</b><br>to publicly declare to be wrong or evil",
            "de- <i>formally</i> + <b>nounce</b> <i>announce</i><br>→ “announce formally (against someone)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>mandate</b><br>an official order; also, authority given by voters",
            "<b>mand</b> <i>order</i> + -ate<br>→ “a thing ordered”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "A word with a silent c",
        "q": "Use the parts: what does it mean to <b>indict</b> someone, and how is it said?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>in-</b> (upon, against) + <b>dict</b> (say).",
          "Literally: “to say against,” to make a formal charge.",
          "The spelling kept the Latin <i>c</i>, but the word is said <b>in-DITE</b>, rhyming with <i>invite</i>."
        ],
        "a": "To formally charge someone with a crime; said in-DITE."
      },
